<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Pacific Fury #5, Shemya Shakedown, 1994</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Pacific Fury 4, Shemya Shakedown, 1994&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;15 Feb 1994.&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This is the fifth scenario of a 16 scenario campaign. Pacific Fury is very closely linked to the Northern Fury campaign. You can explore the situation on the &lt;A href="http://northernfury.bhgdesigns.com/index.php"&gt;webpage&lt;/A&gt;, or&amp;nbsp;read the Northern Fury background document for further insight. The key nuggets&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;UL&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Cold War continued, no thaw in relations. Germany is unified but somewhat unstable, the Warsaw Pact (WP) still active but somewhat less of a force than it was in the 1980s&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Two days ago, 13 Feb 1994 global war broke out between the Soviet Union and NATO along with many western aligned countries.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Both China and North Korea have been extremely quiet and are not participating in any hostilities, although tensions especially with North Korea are high.&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;
&lt;P&gt;You are Commander of the&amp;nbsp;&lt;A href="http://www.ww2.dk/new/navy/143mrad.htm" target=_BLANK&gt;143&lt;SUP&gt;rd&lt;/SUP&gt; Red Banner Missile Aviation Division&lt;/A&gt; based at Mongokhoto Airbase, part of the Soviet Pacific Fleet. In response to an American attack on the Crimea a couple days ago you have been tasked to attack an American base in the Near Islands, part of what the US calls the Aleutian Islands Chain.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Of course, there are a few complications; the Americans have deployed a squadron of F-15s there as part of their NORAD defence, you have the unreliable support of a PVO squadron of MiG-31s, and you must be very careful not to damage their COBRA DANE radar or they will think we are starting a nuclear war.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Designer’s notes&lt;/STRONG&gt;:&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;UL&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Distances are deceptively long; this is the Pacific where everything is big. You have dispersal bases and will need to use them.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;You should turn 'special messages' ON.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;The &lt;A href="http://northernfury.us/warsaw/su/air/" target=_BLANK&gt;Soviet air forces &lt;/A&gt;are four distinct entities, each with their own chain of command, agenda, and priority. Your unit is part of the Navy (VMF), you could argue that this target is more appropriate for the Strategic forces (VA VKG) but they have declined the mission as being too risky to their strategic nuclear deterrent. More problematic however is the relationship with the Air Defence Forces (PVO). You may recall in operations against Hokkaido Japan (Pacific Fury #2) that friction with the PVO was instrumental in putting the entire mission at risk. You will also have support from a squadron of Frontal Aviation (VVS) which will be much more stable.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Points are allotted or lost for targets destroyed and destruction of air forces. You will automatically lose the game if you damage the COBRA DANE radar or the satellite communications infrastructure that supports it.&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
